option.CLOUD_SHADOWS_INTENSITY         = Cloud Shadows Intensity
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS_INTENSITY.comment = Adjusts the intensity of cloud shadows
option.IBL                              = Image Based Lighting
option.IBL.comment                      = Master toggle for Image-Based Lighting (research-driven re-implementation; see include/lighting/ibl.glsl for full technical references).\nWhen enabled, BOTH diffuse and specular IBL are active:\n  - Diffuse: integrates the sky map (colortex4) over the hemisphere around the bent normal using a spherical-Fibonacci low-discrepancy sequence with cosine-weighted importance sampling.  A per-pixel IGN-seeded rotation turns the deterministic pattern into a blue-noise-over-time stochastic sampler so TAA converges the residual Monte-Carlo error.\n  - Specular: VNDF importance-sampled GGX against the live sky map (Heitz 2018, unbiased estimator weight 2*NoL*V2/V1).  When ENVIRONMENT_REFLECTIONS (SSR) is disabled, the entire reflection total is computed by get_ibl_specular().  When SSR is enabled, the existing SSR pipeline runs (which already does proper VNDF multi-sample IBL on SSR misses), so energy is never double-counted.\n  - Mirror fast-path: for near-mirror surfaces (roughness < 0.045), a single bicubic sky tap modulated by the analytical Narkowicz BRDF integration LUT is used.\nAll code is GLSL 4.10 compatible (no compute shaders, no image load/store, no SSBOs).
option.IBL_INTENSITY                    = IBL Diffuse Intensity
option.IBL_INTENSITY.comment            = Scales the diffuse image-based skylight.  The mathematically correct value is pi/N times the average sky radiance; this slider lets you fine-tune the result to match the previous (slightly dimmer) implementation if desired.
option.IBL_SAMPLES                      = IBL Diffuse Samples
option.IBL_SAMPLES.comment              = Number of sky map samples used to integrate diffuse irradiance via the spherical-Fibonacci cosine-weighted sequence.  Higher values capture more sky detail (sun disk, clouds, aurora, horizon gradient) at a greater performance cost.  Recommended: 4 (low) to 32 (ultra).  The per-pixel IGN rotation lets TAA converge the residual error across frames, so even 8 samples looks clean after a few frames.
option.IBL_SPECULAR_INTENSITY           = IBL Specular Intensity
option.IBL_SPECULAR_INTENSITY.comment   = Scales the specular image-based lighting contribution.  Default 1.0 produces physically-correct energy; lower values give a more subtle, less mirror-like look.  Active whenever the IBL master toggle is on; the separate IBL_SPECULAR toggle has been removed in favor of a single IBL master switch.
option.IBL_SPECULAR_SAMPLES             = IBL Specular Samples
option.IBL_SPECULAR_SAMPLES.comment     = Number of VNDF importance-sampled GGX rays traced against the sky map when computing specular IBL (i.e. when ENVIRONMENT_REFLECTIONS is off).  Higher values produce cleaner rough reflections at a greater performance cost.  1 uses the mirror fast-path (single bicubic sky tap + analytical BRDF LUT).  Recommended: 1 (low) to 16 (ultra).  Active whenever the IBL master toggle is on.
