# Misc settings

option.COLOR_OUTPUT_MODE               = Color Output
option.COLOR_OUTPUT_MODE.comment       = Color primaries AND transfer curve baked into the final image before it leaves the shader. sRGB is the safe default for any display. Rec.2020 widens the working gamut toward the output for HDR-capable/wide-gamut monitors (uses the sRGB curve). Display P3 targets Apple's native wide-gamut displays (all modern MacBook/iMac/Studio Display panels) using the sRGB curve. DCI-P3 uses the same P3 primaries but the theatrical 2.6 gamma curve instead - only correct if your display/pipeline expects that curve, otherwise looks too dark/contrasty. Adobe RGB targets pro photo/print-calibrated Mac displays with its own ~2.2 gamma curve. Only looks correct on a display that actually supports the selected space - if colors look oversaturated, too dark, or off, switch back to sRGB.

